Alcohol treatment services encompass professional rehabilitation, intervention, and management programmes designed for individuals struggling with alcohol dependence or misuse. Core components include comprehensive medical assessment, medically supervised withdrawal, behavioural therapy, psychological counselling, peer‑support groups, family‑involvement initiatives, and long‑term after‑care planning. Delivery formats span traditional inpatient facilities, outpatient clinics, community‑based centres, and increasingly, digital platforms that enable remote monitoring and virtual counselling.
